    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>This is a smish-smosh of things related to implementing debug.
It&apos;s all stuffed here to keep the CPU base instruction set as 
clean as possible.
Things here:
* RV5-DEBUG-MODULE: an implementation of the RISC-V debug spec.
* RV5-DEBUG-SYSTEM-PCU: an extension for the PCU that handles 
some system-type instructions as well as certain signals from the
debug module. In a real CPU this would just be part of the PCU.
* System control logic: This is the logic for handling system
instruction decoding and overriding any necessary control signals.
This is another thing that would be in the control logic like anything
else in a real system.
* CSR registers: We need a few CSRs for debug stuff. Those are
defined here.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="-4180" y="-2220"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Rectangle</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>RectHeight</string>
          <int>15</int>
        </entry>
